1. Definitions

"Licensor" means Maviray, which can be contacted at devops@maviray.com.

"Software" means the Maviray.Pdf source code, compiled libraries and NuGet
packages, including the add-on packages whose names begin with
"Maviray.Pdf.", and their documentation, as published by the Licensor,
including updates.

"You" means the individual or legal entity that uses the Software.

"Affiliate" means any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under
common control with You. "Control" means owning more than 50% of the voting
rights, or having the power to direct management.

"Organisation" means You together with all Your Affiliates.

"Annual Gross Revenue" means the Organisation's total gross revenue
(turnover) from all sources in its most recently completed financial year,
as shown in its financial statements. Equity investment and loans are not
revenue. For a public authority, it means the authority's total annual
budget.

"Revenue Threshold" means Annual Gross Revenue of EUR 1,000,000, or the
equivalent in another currency at the exchange rate on the last day of the
financial year concerned.

"Application" means software, a service or a document workflow that You
build, which includes the Software as a component and provides substantial
functionality beyond the Software itself.

"Generated Document" means any file produced by running the Software.


2. Community licence (free of charge)

2.1 Eligibility. You may use the Software under this section without charge
    if at least one of the following applies:

    (a) the Organisation's Annual Gross Revenue is below the Revenue
        Threshold;
    (b) You are an individual using the Software for personal,
        non-commercial purposes;
    (c) You are a registered charity or non-profit organisation using the
        Software for Your non-profit activities, whatever Your revenue;
    (d) You are evaluating the Software, without using it in production,
        for no more than 30 days.

2.2 Grant. Subject to section 4, the Licensor grants You a worldwide,
    non-exclusive, non-transferable and non-sublicensable licence, free of
    charge, to:

    (a) use and copy the Software to develop, test and run Applications;
    (b) modify the Software for use in Your Applications;
    (c) distribute the Software in compiled form as part of Your
        Applications; and
    (d) let the users of Your Applications use the Software as part of
        those Applications.


3. Commercial licence

3.1 If You do not qualify under section 2.1, You need a commercial licence
    from the Licensor to use the Software. A commercial licence is a
    separate written agreement that sets out its fees, scope and term. To
    obtain one, contact the Licensor at devops@maviray.com.

3.2 If the Organisation's Annual Gross Revenue reaches the Revenue Threshold
    while You use the Software under section 2, You may continue under
    section 2 for 90 days after the end of that financial year. To continue
    after that, You need a commercial licence.


